From 856786e638ae9649634889d153203edeba901db9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 02:31:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] http: also redirect NetPass's SpotPass mirror to the custom
 server

NetPass points SpotPass downloads at its own mirror
(https://api.netpass.cafe/npdl/p01/nsa/...), which answers with a 302 to
Nintendo's URL when it doesn't have the file. The BOSS module follows the
redirect but, for the followed request, only checks size and status and
never reads the data (task result 0x5F, error 004-6007 in Disney Magical
World), even though the custom server sent a valid file.

With a custom SpotPass server set, /npdl/ requests to api.netpass.cafe
are now sent to it as well, with the /npdl prefix dropped, so the first
request gets the file directly. The rest of NetPass's API is untouched.
X-Tangelo-Original-Host tells the server which host was meant.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
---
